# .opencode/coord.conf.example — identity defaults for the coordination tools.
#
# Copy to `.opencode/coord.conf` (git-ignored) and fill in your project's values,
# OR pass them as tool args, OR set the matching COORD_* environment variables.
# Precedence: TOOL ARG > COORD_* ENV > this file. The session is always the live
# session (`context.sessionID`) — it cannot be set here.
#
#   agent       the work slug for the `Agent:` line (a stable kebab name for the
#               work, e.g. `ocv2-coordination`; never a harness or account name).
#   harness     the harness name, e.g. OpenCode.
#   model       the provider + model name, e.g. `DeepSeek V4.1 Flash`.
#   confidence  one of the five attribution tiers:
#                 fully tested and validated | analysed on a live system |
#                 documentation reviewed | syntax check only | theoretical suggestion
#
# Every key is optional; a value supplied at the tool call or in the environment
# wins over the one here.

agent=
harness=OpenCode
model=
confidence=
